{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "entity": "gamblee_bonus_research",
  "rules": [
    "One offer object represents exactly one market and one vertical. Multiple simultaneous offers for the same market/vertical are allowed.",
    "Market and currency are independent. A USD-denominated poker offer may target GB, IE or another market.",
    "A multi-stage deposit pack is one offer. Capture all stages in multi_step.rows; structured reward components describe the first stage unless a future schema explicitly models later stages.",
    "Recurring offers remain one offer and use schedule.weekdays and/or validity dates.",
    "Do not output prohibited markets. CA-ON is currently prohibited for public Bonus Offer publication.",
    "If a discovered mechanic cannot be represented exactly by this contract, do not force-fit it. Put it in schema_gaps with status unsupported_but_fixable and propose the exact field/component/type change.",
    "supported_and_analyzable and not_calculable offers may be imported. unsupported_but_fixable items are blocked until the schema is extended.",
    "urls.offer is only for an approved/tracked commercial deep link. Put ordinary official promotion pages in evidence and leave urls.offer null so Gamblee inherits the brand market/vertical commercial link. urls.terms may use a direct official terms URL.",
    "Use excluded_subdivisions for explicit subnational exclusions inside a broader market (for example GB with GB-NIR excluded). Do not hide regional exclusions only in free text.",
    "Prefer current first-party/official evidence. Include source URLs in evidence."
  ],
  "analysis_statuses": [
    "supported_and_analyzable",
    "not_calculable"
